19 cells total with SSIM2 drop ≥ 0.3. All on photo content. Pattern
identical to W44-38 honest-stop: photo SSIM2 drops to chase byte
savings on cells where DCT64 over-fires.

### NEW failure introduced

`imac_g3.png e9 d=3`: encoded fine in baseline (bytes=133047). With
the W44-93 widened gate the encode now exceeds the 2 GiB default
memory budget at e9 (4 butteraugli iters × DCT64 evaluation
infrastructure on 5.6 MP). Verified via `cjxl-rs` CLI:

```
Error encoding: limit exceeded: memory budget exceeded:
requested 202874688 bytes on top of 2079554208 (cap 2147483648)
```

This points to memory pressure that is real but not unbounded. The
budget can be raised; the bench harness uses the default cap. e9 d=3
on 5.6 MP screenshots is a realistic deployment scenario.

## Root cause of the photo SSIM2 regression

Same pattern W44-38 (`8c7644a0`) measured at e6 widening:

> "Photo collateral: SSIM2 -1.31 / -1.54 on 1418519 d=3/4 (bytes
> -1.7% each, status FIXED). Visible photo quality drops to chase a
> screenshot wedge cell that did NOT close."

W44-93 widened to e5 (not e6), and the same regression pattern fires
on 1189261 (-1.21 SSIM2) and 1418519 (-2.22 SSIM2 vs cjxl on e6 d=6).
W44-38 hypothesised "cost-model wedge" via dropped counterweights.
W44-40 MEMORY.md update clarified counterweights ARE on CPU; W44-38's
RC was about GPU encoder. The empirical regression remains valid even
if the diagnostic mechanism was misattributed.

The real cost-model question: when DCT64 is allowed at e5/e6, the
encoder's `EstimateEntropy` over-values the partition's byte savings
without seeing the SSIM2 cost (no butteraugli loop at e5/e6 — gate is
e8+/kKitten per `effort.rs`). At e7+ the cost model gets it right
because either (a) butteraugli loop runs (e8+) or (b) the cells where
DCT64 wins are already in the FIXED band. Widening to e5/e6 exposes
the unrefined cost model on smooth-but-textured photos.

## Why the smart-dispatch in W44-35 doesn't help here

`adapt_to_image_lossy_with_smoothness` (W44-35, `4f8579e7`) was
designed for this exact scenario: smooth photo classifier admits DCT64
on cells where it wins. But the classifier is **gated on
`pixels < 500_000 AND distance < 2.0`** — i.e., it only fires on
small + low-distance cells. The W44-92 wedge cell 1531677 e5 d=6 is
512×512 = 262_144 px (< 500_000) but distance=6.0 (>= 2.0), so the
smart-dispatch doesn't fire and the baseline `try_dct64: effort >= 7`
gate keeps DCT64 off at e5/e6.

The right path forward (NOT shipped in W44-93) is to widen the
smart-dispatch distance window to admit DCT64 on smooth photos at any
distance — or to ship distance-aware DCT64 admission inside the per-
block cost model itself. Both are larger chunks than W44-93's scope.

